    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d111">

                <pb facs="0110" n="98" sameAs="frus:frus1942v04/pg98"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.917 Time/57</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Chief of the Division of Near Eastern
                        Affairs</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Murray</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Under Secretary of
                        State</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Welles</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1942-02-18">February 18, 1942</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Welles</hi>: I discussed this matter with the
                    Egyptian Minister today, and I think I managed to persuade him that it would be
                    better not to give the incident any further publicity.</p>
                <p>The Minister informed me, incidentally, that a representative of <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Time</hi> magazine had come to Washington at his request
                    to discuss the whole question, and that he has been assured that the magazine
                    will make “amends” of some kind in a subsequent issue.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Wallace Murray</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
